# Electrical & Computer Engineering Taste Considerations & Philosophical Probes
#
# Transmuted silicon, the architecture of abstraction, the nanosecond cosmos, and wonder probes across hardware and fields.

#>spw_cache_univ_ece_taste
#:cache #!electrical_and_computer_engineering
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"intent"{
  ~#goal: "Synthesize the aesthetic awe, conceptual architecture, and civilizational responsibility governing electrical and computer engineering."
  ~#resonance: "The transmuting of sand into logic, the layered hierarchy of abstraction, and the physical reality of the digital world"
}

^["the_miracle_of_transmuted_sand"]{
  modern_alchemy: "Humanity took the most abundant, unremarkable material on Earth—beach sand (silicon dioxide)—and through sheer scientific will taught it to calculate, remember, and speak."
  technological_sublime: #[
    "Extreme Ultraviolet Lithography (EUV): Directing 13.5 nm wavelength photons bouncing off atomic-precision multilayer mirrors to etch patterns narrower than a strand of human DNA",
    "Trillion-Transistor Monoliths: Packing more functional active switches onto a thumbnail-sized die of silicon than there are stars in our galaxy",
    "Quantum Tunneling Defiance: Holding back electrons whose wavefunctions naturally wish to leak across barriers only three atoms thick"
  ]
}

^["the_poetry_of_the_abstraction_stack"]{
  intellectual_triumph: "The greatest intellectual construct in human history is the computer engineering abstraction stack."
  hierarchy: #[
    "Quantum Bandgaps & Fermi Levels (Physics) -> Drift and Diffusion in Semiconductors (Device Physics)",
    "Small-Signal Models & Biasing (Analog Circuits) -> Threshold Voltages & Inverters (Digital Gates)",
    "Boolean Switching Logic (Logic Design) -> Register Transfer Level State Machines (Microarchitecture)",
    "Instruction Set Architectures (ISA) -> Compilers & Operating Systems (Systems Software)",
    "The Invariant Beauty: Each layer is completely insulated from the layer below it, allowing a software engineer to write an algorithm without knowing whether electrons are flowing through silicon, gallium nitride, or vacuum tubes"
  ]
}

^["the_ethics_of_the_digital_chassis"]{
  civilizational_vulnerability: "Human society has placed its entire financial system, power grid, medical records, and supply chains onto microscopic silicon chips."
  grave_responsibilities: #[
    "Hardware Root of Trust: Ensuring that the silicon itself is free of hardware Trojans, side-channel leakage (Spectre, Meltdown), and manufacturing backdoors",
    "The Heat of Thought: Acknowledging that global computing now consumes over 2% of world electricity; computer engineers have an ecological duty to optimize energy per flop",
    "Digital Fragility: Remembering that a single coronal mass ejection from the sun could induce grid-collapsing geomagnetic currents across high-voltage transformer lines"
  ]
}

^"taste"{
  ~#taste: "Electrical and computer engineering is the realization that the boundary between physical matter and pure thought is an engineering problem."
  ~#wonder: "Why does the physical universe permit discrete, error-free Boolean computation to exist in a macroscopic world that is continuous, noisy, and hot?"
}

^"invariants"{
  "Engineers must ensure that digital systems maintain fail-safe operational behavior under unexpected voltage brownouts or clock glitches.",
  "Hardware designs for critical safety infrastructure must isolate safety-critical control planes from untrusted network interfaces.",
  "Computer architecture benchmarks must report energy expenditure (Joules per task) alongside throughput or latency.",
}

#>wonder_ece_taste_1
?["Can neuromorphic event-based spiking silicon match the biological energy efficiency of the human brain (20 Watts)?"]{
  #:depth #!biological ~#lens(neuromorphic_computing)
  ~#hypothesis: "Asynchronous event-driven spiking neural architectures using memristive crossbars compute sensor-motor inference with 100x lower energy dissipation than synchronous von Neumann GPUs by computing only when input data changes."
  !probe{ "Measure energy consumption per inference in sub-threshold analog memristor networks vs quantized GPU tensor cores on auditory localization tasks." }
  $%[neuromorphic.energy_per_spike_picojoules, latency.event_response_microseconds]
}

#>wonder_ece_taste_2
?["What is the fundamental thermodynamic and quantum limit to how small a silicon transistor can be made before thermal noise destroys digital state?"]{
  #:depth #!physical ~#lens(subthreshold_quantum_limits)
  ~#hypothesis: "At gate lengths below 1.5 nanometers, direct source-to-drain Heisenberg quantum tunneling exceeds subthreshold drift current, establishing an inescapable quantum limit where classical Boolean logic must transition to quantum probabilistic or topological computing."
  !probe{ "Simulate and measure non-equilibrium Green's function (NEGF) quantum transport through 1nm silicon and 2D transition-metal nanosheets." }
  $%[devices.subthreshold_swing_mv_decade, quantum.tunneling_leakage_current_density]
}
